course: dictionary
lesson: 1660
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. A chisel is a tool, but chisel can also be a verb: to chisel means to cut or carve with a chisel. «He chiselled his name into the stone.» Here the sentence shows an action, so chiselled is the verb.
explain: Look at the words around the word. «Each front tooth has hard enamel at the front and softer stuff at the back, so gnawing wears the back faster and keeps a chisel edge.» There is no tool here. A chisel edge is a sharp, flat edge like the end of a chisel. Try the tool meaning in the sentence and it does not fit, so the meaning must be about shape.
explain: A word can change its form too. «Chiselled» features means a face with sharp, clear lines, so in a story a chiselled face is handsome and strong. Ask yourself: is this word a tool, an action, or a description? The answer shows which meaning to use.
fact: A chisel is a tool with a flat, sharp metal end, used with a hammer or mallet to cut or shape wood, stone or metal.
fact: «Chisel» can also be a verb, meaning to cut or carve with a chisel.
fact: «Chiselled» features means a face with sharp, clear lines.
fact: Sculptors and stonemasons use chisels to carve statues and letters, so you may meet chisels in history and design and technology lessons.
fact: In old US slang, «chisel» can mean to cheat someone, so always check the context.
exercise: «He chiselled his name into the stone.» In this sentence, what does chiselled mean? | Washed clean with water | *Cut or carved with a chisel | Lost in the mud | Painted in bright colours
exercise: A chisel has a flat, sharp metal end. What is a chisel? | *A tool used with a hammer to cut wood, stone or metal | A small dish for soup | A kind of bird with a long beak
exercise: Safety first: «Always cut away from your body.» When you use a chisel, where should your hands be? | Waving in the air to keep warm | *Behind the blade, away from the cutting edge | Holding the wood right under the blade
test: «Each front tooth has hard enamel at the front and softer stuff at the back, so gnawing keeps a chisel edge.» In this sentence, a chisel edge means | A dirty mark on the enamel | A tool for cutting a tooth | A soft, round edge like a pillow | *A sharp, flat edge like the end of a chisel
test: «His chiselled face looked strong and handsome in the story.» What does chiselled mean here? | *Having sharp, clear lines | Covered in tiny holes | Covered in dust from carving | Cut into pieces
exam: In «the first cans were opened with a hammer and chisel», what is a chisel? | A type of can | A kind of food | *A tool with a flat, sharp metal end | A cook's bowl
